Cut 2026-10-28 on Anthony's word ("prepare the release"), in PR release/v0.93.0. The tag push stays his. A minor carrying:
- #804: every typed edge tool's description names draw_edges' real argument (edges); a check fails the build when a served description names an argument its tool does not take;
- #805: propagate_change budget_chars, propagate_change / propagate_from paging with offset; loop_status gives list rows to its budget before prose; set_violation_status resolved_at, violates_rule detected_at; the redo list follows DOCUMENTS; no served text names record_change;
- #806: add_inference held_as (supposition / principle / model); reasoning_report keeps its summary room; create_node / create_nodes near_match_check;
- #807: the design-a-phenomenon skill;
- #808: the owner's signed ruling (a Decision conceding a result, accepted with an approver) refutes by a named result; a claim a result supports, resting otherwise only on what is held on purpose, reads supported given it;
- #809: server-time write stamps sealed with HMAC-SHA256 under a key kept in the store; reasoning_report prediction_order; export_graph stamps: true.

Measured against the published 0.92.0 binary (linux-x86_64 archive sha256 7720cf66..., checked against checksums.txt): 199 tools on both, none added or removed, 38 differ additively (new arguments on add_inference, export_graph, propagate_change, propagate_from, set_violation_status, violates_rule; descriptions on 32). Skills 34 -> 35 (design-a-phenomenon added; design-a-proof and design-an-argument changed in their words). get_instructions unchanged. Nothing deprecated or removed. The schema stamp does not move (28 node, 69 edge types, node vocabulary unchanged; PREMISE_OF gains the edge property held_as), so no upgrade doc is owed. Write cost of the stamps: no measurable change on single writes (NVMe 75-79 ms on both, flush-bound; RAM disk within 0.05 ms), a 100-node batch 11.3 -> 12.5 ms on a RAM disk; +182 bytes of store per stamped node. Rollback: 0.92.0 opens a store this release wrote (behind warning) and shows the three stamps as ordinary properties in get_node, scan_nodes, receipts and its exports; its writes carry them forward and this release then reads them as imported. Timings on reflow2's own design, median of 3 one-shot reads on an i5-10300H, 0.92.0 -> 0.93.0: loop_status 8.1 -> 8.1 s (reply 29,641 -> 23,868 chars), reasoning_report 1.30 -> 1.26 s, detect_gaps 4.05 -> 3.97 s, graph_report 7.10 -> 6.77 s. Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018ibUbMKCS1yK5W17cncp9P
